The  driver provides support for Intel(R) PRO/Wireless 2200BG and
2915ABG MiniPCI network adapters.  By default, the driver config‐
ures the adapter for BSS  operation  (aka  infrastructure  mode).
This mode requires the use of an access point.  For more informa‐
tion  on configuring this device, see The Intel firmware requires
acceptance of the End User License Agreement.  The  full  license
text  can  be  found  in  The license is agreed to by setting the
sysctl variable to 1.  Join an existing BSS network  (i.e.:  con‐
nect  to  an access point): Join a specific BSS network with net‐
work name Join a specific BSS network with 64  bits  WEP  encryp‐
tion:  ifconfig  iwi0  inet  192.168.0.20 netmask 0xffffff00 nwid
my_net \
        nwkey 0x1234567890  Join  a  specific  BSS  network  with
128bits  WEP  encryption: ifconfig iwi0 inet 192.168.0.20 netmask
0xffffff00 nwid my_net \
        nwkey 0x01020304050607080910111213 The driver will  reset
the  hardware.   This should not happen.  The driver and this man
